<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Was it for sins that I had done</l><l>He groaned upon the tree?</l><l>Amazing pity! grace unknown!</l><l>And love beyond degree!</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Well might the sun in darkness hide,</l><l>And shut his glories in,</l><l>When the incarnate Maker died</l><l>For man, His creature’s sin.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Thus might I hide my blushing face</l><l>While His dear cross appears</l><l>Dissolve my heart in thankfulness,</l><l>And melt mine eyes to tears.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>But drops of grief can ne’er repay</l><l>The debt of love I owe;</l><l>Here Lord, I give myself away:</l><l>’Tis all that I can do.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
